 From all the questions you've been asking lately it would seem like 
you're new to Tru64, and hacking away at it won't make it work any 
better.  I'd suggest reading one of the Administration guides for a 
start to understand the OS better.

Anyways, that route is an interface route and supposed to be there, I 
assume you have an address in that subnet, for example 1.1.X.X ?  You 
shouldn't be deleting the route.  Since it's getting added back 
automatically that means you're running a routing daemon - either gated 
or routed, I'll guess it's routed from the snippet you gave.  Also, why 
do you have this route:

 > 1.1.0.0          1.11.4.4           UGHS        0        0  tu1

You've added it by hand, but it's unnecessary as the default route is 
really all you need since they're both pointing at the same gateway.

