including Ultrix) have the annoying feature to simply ignore
explitic rules stated in a makefile. With a construct like e.g. (excerpt):

LIB = libxxx.a
.c.a:
         $(CC) -c $(CFLAGS) $<
         ar -rv  $@ $*.o
         rm -f $*.o
$(LIB)(myfile.o) : myfile.c

I would expect that "myfile" would be compiled and
subsequently be archived in the given library.
At least this is the way it works on half a dozen
other Unices. Not so on Tru64, it just compiles
but doesn't archive. Very annoying.
I tried to follow the man pages, which say
that rules can be put into a "Makeconf" file,
but this is ignored as well.

Any ideas out there ?



